Functions:
```gdscript
# ---------- SPIKE-001-FIX-002: drag mode (key 4=A / key 5=B), FPS control (key 7), input accumulation (key 6) ----------

func _set_drag_mode(mode: String) -> void:
	_drag_mode = mode
	# On switch, reset drag state to avoid cross-mode residue (§3.1).
	_drag_pending = false
	_dragging = false
	_native_drag_active = false
	_log_event("drag_mode:%s" % ("a" if mode == "A" else "b"))
	_update_status()


func _toggle_fps_cap() -> void:
	# SDD-175: the canonical default is 30; key 7 only provides a runtime 60 control for a single GUI session, does not change after restart.
	Engine.max_fps = 60 if Engine.max_fps != 60 else 30
	_log_event("fps_cap_toggle:%d" % Engine.max_fps)
	_update_status()


func _toggle_accumulated_input() -> void:
	# §9.5 experiment: use_accumulated_input=true (engine default) merges mouse motion per frame → A-mode window position update is capped by frame rate.
	if not _accum_input_supported:
		_log_event("accum_input_unsupported:Input.use_accumulated_input")
		return
	Input.use_accumulated_input = not Input.use_accumulated_input
	_log_event("accum_input:%s" % ("on" if Input.use_accumulated_input else "off"))
	_update_status()
```

_start_native_drag:
```gdscript
func _start_native_drag(note: String) -> bool:
	if not _window_start_drag_supported:
		if not _drag_unsupported_logged:
			_drag_unsupported_logged = true
			_log_event("drag_b_unsupported:DisplayServer.window_start_drag")
		return false
	var wid := 0
	if _window_get_window_id_supported:
		wid = int(_win.call("get_window_id"))
	else:
		# §3.1 probe-based fallback: if Window.get_window_id is missing, pass 0 (main window) and log honestly.
		_log_event("drag_b_window_id_fallback:0")
	DisplayServer.window_start_drag(wid)
	_native_drag_active = true
	_drag_pending = false
	_dragging = false
	_native_drag_samples = []
	_native_drag_sample_count = 0
	_log_event("native_drag_start:%s" % note)
	_update_status()
	return true
```

Hmm wait — on fallback to A in B mode: plan says "when missing, _log_event("drag_b_unsupported") and auto-handle with scheme A behavior, no silent degradation". So in B mode if unsupported: fall through to A behavior (manual move). _drag_unsupported_logged is reused (reset in press branch). Good.

_end_native_drag:
```gdscript
func _end_native_drag() -> void:
	if not _native_drag_active:
		return
	var net := Vector2(_win.position - _drag_start_win).length()
	if net < DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX:
		# §9.2 B-mode post-hoc threshold judgment: net displacement <6px → count as click (README documents the semantic difference explicitly).
		_ship_clicks += 1
		_log_event("ship_click:native_b_postcheck")
	_log_event("native_drag_end:samples=%d:net_px=%.1f" % [_native_drag_sample_count, net])
	_native_drag_active = false
	_save_position()
	_write_reports()
	_update_status()
```

Hmm wait — event names: plan §3.2 says "log native_drag_end". Plan B-fallback: "on drag end, if net window displacement <6px, count as click (ship_clicks+1)". My event "ship_click:native_b_postcheck" — A-mode event is exactly "ship_click". To keep event parsing consistent, log "ship_click" and then "native_drag_end:...". Let's log "ship_click" and "native_drag_end:samples=%d:net_px=%d" separately. Cleaner.

